# AI/ML-Based Real-Time Stock Screening & Trade Filtering

## Objective

A Python-based real-time stock screening and paper-trading system using:

- SMMA 20
- SMMA 120
- LTQ
- Bid/Ask market depth
- Bid/Ask imbalance
- Machine Learning
- Paper trading

## Strategy

Stocks are screened using:

- NSE stocks
- LTP between ₹30 and ₹500
- Bid quantity > 10 lakh
- Ask quantity > 10 lakh
- 1-minute timeframe

A BUY signal occurs when SMMA20 crosses above SMMA120.

A SELL signal occurs when SMMA20 crosses below SMMA120.

The ML model evaluates the crossover using market microstructure and technical features.

## ML Features

- Price returns
- Volume change
- LTQ change
- LTQ acceleration
- Bid quantity change
- Ask quantity change
- Bid/Ask imbalance
- Imbalance change
- Bid/Ask spread
- Price-to-book distances
- SMMA spread
- SMMA slopes

## Decision

Probability >= 65%:

ACCEPT

Probability < 65%:

AVOID

## Paper Trading

No real-money orders are placed.

The system records:

- Entry
- Exit
- P/L
- Exit reason
- Signal
- ML probability

## Validation

Day-1 data is used to train the model.

The trained model is frozen.

Day-2 data is used for validation without retraining before prediction.

## Security

API credentials must be stored in `.env`.

Never commit `.env` to GitHub.
